==English==

===Etymology===
[[Eponym]] after Gerard Kuiper, who [[theorized]] about the belt's existence.

===Pronunciation===
(KYE-per belt OB-jekt)

===Noun===
{{en-noun|sg=[[Kuiper]] [[belt|Belt]] [[object|Object]]}}

# A type of [[trans-Neptunian object]] (TNO) (a certain type of [[minor planet]]) that has an orbit in the Kuiper belt (between 30-50 AU) with [[inclination|inclinations]] consistent with the [[ecliptic]].

